The round is complete: implementation finalized and verified (20 single-call configs + 13 chain gates all PASS on the scoring node), and the strategy record has a full Round d1_r3 section documenting the wins, the dead ends with numbers, and the measurement lessons (thermal drift, the inlining/attribute gotchas, the mmap hugepage fix).

**Technique ended on:** Agarwal–Cooley coprime-2D Bluestein with a node-retuned minimal-M split (65537→1024×135, odd axis extended to 135), split-width codegen (zmm for L2-resident conv kernels — after discovering gcc silently drops `prefer-vector-width=512` when inlining, ymm for the L3-bound single-pass), NT-streamed exit scatter, tile-spread software prefetch, and fully pre-faulted mmap hugepage planes with cross-block L2 skew. Best Ice Lake scoring-node numbers (wallaby unused this round — the real node was finally available): **10007: 180 us B=1 / 192 us B=64; 100003: 2660 us B=1 (beats FFTW-patient's 2713) / 2822 us B=8; 65537: 2008 us B=1 (was 3868); rel L2 ≤ 1.3e-15** (tol 1e-12), chain gates pass with four decades of margin.
